    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d418">

                <pb facs="0456" n="372" sameAs="frus:frus1918Supp02/pg372"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. No. 815.156/2</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to the Minister in
                        Honduras</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Ewing</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1917-09-29T18:00:00-05:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">September 29, 1917, 6 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Mr. Casey, of W. R. Grace &amp; Co., has been authorized by Mr. Rosseter, of the
                    Pacific Mail, to sound the Government of Honduras regarding development of the
                    port at San Lorenzo. Casey should leave Salvador in October, spending the 4th
                    and 5th at Tegucigalpa. Believe he wants port concession on Sacate Grande
                    Island.</p>
                <p>In view of conditions, Department desires you to use every possible proper effort
                    to advance interests of American commerce.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Polk</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
